TITLE: foodcode-onion
FCM: NON-DROP FRAME

001  AX       V     C        00:00:00:00 00:00:03:20 00:00:00:00 00:00:03:20
* FROM CLIP NAME: PAY ATTENTION
* VISUAL: A hand building a sandwich with a big red arrow pointing at it
* NARRATION: The next time you make a sandwich, pay attention to this one thing.

002  AX       V     C        00:00:03:20 00:00:07:12 00:00:03:20 00:00:07:12
* FROM CLIP NAME: UNDER 30 MINUTES
* VISUAL: A knife slicing an onion beside a stopwatch reading thirty minutes
* NARRATION: Slicing one raw onion can change the speed of your blood in under thirty minutes.

003  AX       V     C        00:00:07:12 00:00:10:32 00:00:07:12 00:00:10:32
* FROM CLIP NAME: IN MINUTES
* VISUAL: A calendar with weeks crossed out, a stopwatch with minutes circled
* NARRATION: Not eventually, not over weeks of eating better. In minutes, while you eat.

004  AX       V     C        00:00:10:32 00:00:13:53 00:00:10:32 00:00:13:53
* FROM CLIP NAME: EVERY SINGLE DAY
* VISUAL: A crowd of people of different ages all eating onions, none aware
* NARRATION: Most people your age eat onions almost every single day without knowing this.

005  AX       V     C        00:00:13:53 00:00:17:29 00:00:13:53 00:00:17:29
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOBODY KNOWS
* VISUAL: Three generations at a table with onions, all with question marks above
* NARRATION: Your parents ate them. Your grandparents ate them. Almost nobody knows what they do.

006  AX       V     C        00:00:17:29 00:00:21:35 00:00:17:29 00:00:21:35
* FROM CLIP NAME: MOST MISUNDERSTOOD
* VISUAL: A globe with onions scattered over every continent, a question mark
* NARRATION: It is one of the most common foods on earth and one of the most misunderstood.

007  AX       V     C        00:00:21:35 00:00:25:27 00:00:21:35 00:00:25:27
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOUR LAST MEAL
* VISUAL: A burger with onion rings peeking out, a thought bubble above
* NARRATION: Think about your last meal with onions in it. Maybe it was on a burger.

008  AX       V     C        00:00:25:27 00:00:28:47 00:00:25:27 00:00:28:47
* FROM CLIP NAME: RAW ON A SALAD
* VISUAL: Raw onion rings scattered on a salad bowl, half hidden under leaves
* NARRATION: Maybe it was raw, scattered on top of a salad you barely noticed.

009  AX       V     C        00:00:28:47 00:00:31:53 00:00:28:47 00:00:31:53
* FROM CLIP NAME: INTO THE SAUCE
* VISUAL: Onion pieces falling into a simmering sauce pan, unnoticed
* NARRATION: Maybe you chopped one into a sauce without ever tasting it directly.

010  AX       V     C        00:00:31:53 00:00:34:58 00:00:31:53 00:00:34:58
* FROM CLIP NAME: JUST THERE
* VISUAL: A plate with an onion shrugging quietly in the corner
* NARRATION: You probably did not think twice about it. Onions are just there.

011  AX       V     C        00:00:34:58 00:00:38:50 00:00:34:58 00:00:38:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: BACKGROUND NOISE
* VISUAL: A hand pushing an onion slice to the edge of a plate
* NARRATION: Background noise on a plate. A garnish you push aside if you dislike the crunch.

012  AX       V     C        00:00:38:50 00:00:42:10 00:00:38:50 00:00:42:10
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE PROBLEM
* VISUAL: An onion wearing a Superman cape nobody is looking at
* NARRATION: Nobody treats an onion like something powerful. And that is exactly the problem.

013  AX       V     C        00:00:42:10 00:00:45:31 00:00:42:10 00:00:45:31
* FROM CLIP NAME: WE EXPECT DRAMA
* VISUAL: A shelf of exotic glowing fruit with dramatic spotlights
* NARRATION: We are trained to think powerful foods must look dramatic or taste exotic.

014  AX       V     C        00:00:45:31 00:00:49:37 00:00:45:31 00:00:49:37
* FROM CLIP NAME: EXPENSIVE PROMISES
* VISUAL: A supplement bottle covered in promise words and a large price sticker
* NARRATION: Or arrive in a bottle with a label full of promises and a matching price tag.

015  AX       V     C        00:00:49:37 00:00:53:29 00:00:49:37 00:00:53:29
* FROM CLIP NAME: SITTING IGNORED
* VISUAL: A glowing compound molecule sitting alone on a kitchen counter
* NARRATION: Meanwhile one of the most active compounds you can swallow sits ignored in your kitchen.

016  AX       V     C        00:00:53:29 00:00:57:20 00:00:53:29 00:00:57:20
* FROM CLIP NAME: LESS THAN A DOLLAR
* VISUAL: An onion on a shop shelf with a price tag reading under one dollar
* NARRATION: Sitting in almost every kitchen on earth, completely ignored, selling for less than a dollar.

017  AX       V     C        00:00:57:20 00:01:00:41 00:00:57:20 00:01:00:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: BILLIONS SPENT
* VISUAL: A mountain of money with a heart shape and pill bottles on top
* NARRATION: Think how much money gets spent every year on heart health supplements alone.

018  AX       V     C        00:01:00:41 00:01:03:46 00:01:00:41 00:01:03:46
* FROM CLIP NAME: PILLS AND POWDERS
* VISUAL: Pills and powder tubs with arrows pointing at a healthy heart diagram
* NARRATION: Pills promising better circulation, powders promising to support your entire cardiovascular system.

019  AX       V     C        00:01:03:46 00:01:07:38 00:01:03:46 00:01:07:38
* FROM CLIP NAME: FREE ALREADY
* VISUAL: A factory processing plant beside a free vegetable, price tags compared
* NARRATION: Most of them contain, in processed and expensive form, compounds your body could get free.

020  AX       V     C        00:01:07:38 00:01:10:58 00:01:07:38 00:01:10:58
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU OWN IT
* VISUAL: A person walking past an onion bowl in their own kitchen
* NARRATION: From a vegetable you almost certainly already own and walk past every week.

021  AX       V     C        00:01:10:58 00:01:14:34 00:01:10:58 00:01:14:34
* FROM CLIP NAME: QUERCETIN
* VISUAL: An onion cut open revealing a glowing molecule labelled quercetin
* NARRATION: Here is what almost nobody knows. Inside that onion is a compound called quercetin.

022  AX       V     C        00:01:14:34 00:01:17:55 00:01:14:34 00:01:17:55
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE INNER LINING
* VISUAL: A quercetin molecule travelling toward the wall of a blood vessel
* NARRATION: Quercetin does something very specific to the inner lining of your blood vessels.

023  AX       V     C        00:01:17:55 00:01:22:01 00:01:17:55 00:01:22:01
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE ENDOTHELIUM
* VISUAL: A blood vessel wall highlighted with a name tag reading endothelium
* NARRATION: That lining has a name. It is called the endothelium, and it is not passive plumbing.

024  AX       V     C        00:01:22:01 00:01:25:53 00:01:22:01 00:01:25:53
* FROM CLIP NAME: ACTIVE TISSUE
* VISUAL: A vessel cross-section widening and narrowing like a camera aperture
* NARRATION: It is a thin layer of cells controlling how wide or narrow your vessels are.

025  AX       V     C        00:01:25:53 00:01:29:13 00:01:25:53 00:01:29:13
* FROM CLIP NAME: CONSTANT DECISIONS
* VISUAL: Endothelial cells as little workers pulling levers to control flow
* NARRATION: Active tissue, making constant decisions about how your blood should move right now.

026  AX       V     C        00:01:29:13 00:01:32:34 00:01:29:13 00:01:32:34
* FROM CLIP NAME: NITRIC OXIDE
* VISUAL: Quercetin docking into a cell and tiny nitric oxide bubbles bursting out
* NARRATION: When quercetin reaches those cells, it triggers them to release more nitric oxide.

027  AX       V     C        00:01:32:34 00:01:36:10 00:01:32:34 00:01:36:10
* FROM CLIP NAME: RELAX AND WIDEN
* VISUAL: A nitric oxide molecule holding a megaphone, vessel walls relaxing outward
* NARRATION: Nitric oxide is the signal that tells your blood vessels to relax and widen.

028  AX       V     C        00:01:36:10 00:01:39:30 00:01:36:10 00:01:39:30
* FROM CLIP NAME: FASTER FLOW
* VISUAL: Red blood cells racing smoothly through a wide open vessel tunnel
* NARRATION: Wider vessels mean blood moves faster, with less pressure and far less strain.

029  AX       V     C        00:01:39:30 00:01:43:06 00:01:39:30 00:01:43:06
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE STUDY
* VISUAL: A journal cover reading Journal of Nutrition with a vascular function graph improving
* NARRATION: A study in the Journal of Nutrition found dietary quercetin measurably improved vascular function.

030  AX       V     C        00:01:43:06 00:01:46:11 00:01:43:06 00:01:46:11
* FROM CLIP NAME: MEASURED IN HUMANS
* VISUAL: A body outline with nitric oxide levels rising on a gauge
* NARRATION: It did that by increasing nitric oxide availability inside the living body.

031  AX       V     C        00:01:46:11 00:01:50:03 00:01:46:11 00:01:50:03
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT A GUESS
* VISUAL: A stack of peer reviewed papers with multiple stamp approvals
* NARRATION: That is not a guess. It is documented, peer reviewed, and repeated across research groups.

032  AX       V     C        00:01:50:03 00:01:53:08 00:01:50:03 00:01:53:08
* FROM CLIP NAME: REPEATED
* VISUAL: Three separate lab teams in different rooms all getting matching results
* NARRATION: Multiple independent teams looking at the same mechanism found the same result.

033  AX       V     C        00:01:53:08 00:01:56:44 00:01:53:08 00:01:56:44
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU NEVER FEEL IT
* VISUAL: A person sleeping peacefully while their vessels tighten unseen
* NARRATION: This matters more than people realize because you never feel your vascular function directly.

034  AX       V     C        00:01:56:44 00:02:00:05 00:01:56:44 00:02:00:05
* FROM CLIP NAME: SILENT FOR YEARS
* VISUAL: Someone waking up with a speech bubble about tight endothelium, confused
* NARRATION: You do not wake up thinking, my endothelium seems unusually tight this morning.

035  AX       V     C        00:02:00:05 00:02:03:41 00:02:00:05 00:02:03:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: UNTIL IT DOESN'T
* VISUAL: A silent ticking clock with a vessel slowly narrowing over a decade
* NARRATION: It works silently in the background for years, until the day it does not.

036  AX       V     C        00:02:03:41 00:02:07:32 00:02:03:41 00:02:07:32
* FROM CLIP NAME: DECADES IN THE MAKING
* VISUAL: An iceberg with most of the damage hidden below the waterline
* NARRATION: By the time people notice something is wrong, the process has been building for decades.

037  AX       V     C        00:02:07:32 00:02:10:53 00:02:07:32 00:02:10:53
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE GARDEN HOSE
* VISUAL: A garden hose pinched by a giant thumb, water trickling weakly
* NARRATION: Picture a garden hose that has been pinched halfway shut by a thumb.

038  AX       V     C        00:02:10:53 00:02:14:13 00:02:10:53 00:02:14:13
* FROM CLIP NAME: STRAINING THE HOSE
* VISUAL: The pinched hose bulging with pressure, strain marks along the rubber
* NARRATION: Water still comes out, but slower, with more pressure straining the hose itself.

039  AX       V     C        00:02:14:13 00:02:17:19 00:02:14:13 00:02:17:19
* FROM CLIP NAME: RELEASE THE PINCH
* VISUAL: The thumb lifting off the hose, water gushing out smoothly
* NARRATION: Now picture someone releasing that pinch. The water flows freer, calmer, easier.

040  AX       V     C        00:02:17:19 00:02:20:39 00:02:17:19 00:02:20:39
* FROM CLIP NAME: IN YOUR ARTERIES
* VISUAL: An artery relaxing open with quercetin molecules cheering it on
* NARRATION: That is what happens in your arteries when quercetin does its job properly.

041  AX       V     C        00:02:20:39 00:02:24:46 00:02:20:39 00:02:24:46
* FROM CLIP NAME: LESS WORK FOR YOUR HEART
* VISUAL: A relaxed heart lifting a light feather instead of a heavy weight
* NARRATION: Your heart does not have to fight as hard to push blood through an open system.

042  AX       V     C        00:02:24:46 00:02:28:22 00:02:24:46 00:02:28:22
* FROM CLIP NAME: AFTER A MEAL
* VISUAL: A person slumped at a table after eating, fog clouds over their head
* NARRATION: Have you ever felt sluggish after a meal, foggy, like your brain is starving?

043  AX       V     C        00:02:28:22 00:02:31:42 00:02:28:22 00:02:31:42
* FROM CLIP NAME: TOO TIGHT
* VISUAL: A narrowed vessel with a red warning band squeezing it shut
* NARRATION: Part of that might be exactly this. Vessels tighter than they should be.

044  AX       V     C        00:02:31:42 00:02:35:02 00:02:31:42 00:02:35:02
* FROM CLIP NAME: STARVED OF OXYGEN
* VISUAL: A brain with a thin oxygen supply line, a dimming light bulb above
* NARRATION: Restricting flow to the places that need oxygen the most, your brain included.

045  AX       V     C        00:02:35:02 00:02:38:23 00:02:35:02 00:02:38:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT JUST QUERCETIN
* VISUAL: An onion with two glowing compartments, quercetin and something unknown
* NARRATION: Here is the part that surprises people more. Onions are not just quercetin.

046  AX       V     C        00:02:38:23 00:02:41:59 00:02:38:23 00:02:41:59
* FROM CLIP NAME: SULFUR COMPOUNDS
* VISUAL: A knife breaking onion cell walls, little sulfur molecules flying out
* NARRATION: When you cut into one, the cell walls break open and sulfur compounds escape.

047  AX       V     C        00:02:41:59 00:02:45:19 00:02:41:59 00:02:45:19
* FROM CLIP NAME: WHY YOU CRY
* VISUAL: A person chopping onions with tears streaming down their face
* NARRATION: These are the same compounds that make you cry while you are chopping.

048  AX       V     C        00:02:45:19 00:02:49:11 00:02:45:19 00:02:49:11
* FROM CLIP NAME: FROM IRRITANT TO ALLY
* VISUAL: Sulfur molecules arriving at the blood stream, an alarm turning into a green light
* NARRATION: Your body treats them almost like an irritant at first contact, and then something changes.

049  AX       V     C        00:02:49:11 00:02:52:47 00:02:49:11 00:02:52:47
* FROM CLIP NAME: PLATELETS
* VISUAL: Platelets floating apart instead of sticking together in clumps
* NARRATION: Once those compounds reach your bloodstream, they reduce how much your platelets clump together.

050  AX       V     C        00:02:52:47 00:02:56:23 00:02:52:47 00:02:56:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: UP TO 30%
* VISUAL: A big bold number thirty percent with a downward red arrow
* NARRATION: We are talking about a reduction of up to thirty percent in platelet aggregation.

051  AX       V     C        00:02:56:23 00:02:59:43 00:02:56:23 00:02:59:43
* FROM CLIP NAME: THINNER BLOOD
* VISUAL: Two blood samples side by side, one thick and one flowing freely
* NARRATION: Thirty percent. Your blood is literally thinner an hour after you eat it.

052  AX       V     C        00:02:59:43 00:03:03:04 00:02:59:43 00:03:03:04
* FROM CLIP NAME: ALLIUM VEGETABLES
* VISUAL: A review paper with garlic, onion and leek drawings on the cover
* NARRATION: That number comes from a review of allium vegetables and their cardiovascular effects.

053  AX       V     C        00:03:03:04 00:03:06:09 00:03:03:04 00:03:06:09
* FROM CLIP NAME: PEER REVIEWED
* VISUAL: A cardiology journal beside a crumpled supplement brochure in a bin
* NARRATION: Published in a peer reviewed cardiology journal, not a supplement company brochure.

054  AX       V     C        00:03:06:09 00:03:09:45 00:03:06:09 00:03:09:45
* FROM CLIP NAME: THEIR REAL JOB
* VISUAL: A cut on a finger with platelets rushing in to form a plug
* NARRATION: Why does that matter? Because platelets are supposed to help you when you bleed.

055  AX       V     C        00:03:09:45 00:03:13:05 00:03:09:45 00:03:13:05
* FROM CLIP NAME: FORM A BARRIER
* VISUAL: Platelets linking arms to build a wall across a wound
* NARRATION: That is their job. Clump together, form a barrier, stop the damage quickly.

056  AX       V     C        00:03:13:05 00:03:16:41 00:03:13:05 00:03:16:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: WHEN THERE'S NO CUT
* VISUAL: Platelets clumping inside an intact vessel, forming a dangerous clog
* NARRATION: But clumping when you are not bleeding is what leads to blockages and clots.

057  AX       V     C        00:03:16:41 00:03:20:17 00:03:16:41 00:03:20:17
* FROM CLIP NAME: NO WARNING
* VISUAL: An ambulance and emergency room doors with a sudden alarm light
* NARRATION: The kind of events that put people in emergency rooms with almost no warning.

058  AX       V     C        00:03:20:17 00:03:24:09 00:03:20:17 00:03:24:09
* FROM CLIP NAME: RIGHT NOW
* VISUAL: A clock face showing blood cells crawling slowly through a vessel
* NARRATION: Your blood right now might be thicker and slower than it actually needs to be.

059  AX       V     C        00:03:24:09 00:03:27:45 00:03:24:09 00:03:27:45
* FROM CLIP NAME: JUST YEARS
* VISUAL: A long timeline of ordinary meals with vessels quietly narrowing
* NARRATION: Not from anything dramatic you did. Just years of never supporting your blood vessels.

060  AX       V     C        00:03:27:45 00:03:31:37 00:03:27:45 00:03:31:37
* FROM CLIP NAME: IN YOUR DRAWER
* VISUAL: A kitchen drawer opening to reveal a single glowing raw onion
* NARRATION: And a raw onion sitting in your kitchen drawer right now can start changing that.

061  AX       V     C        00:03:31:37 00:03:34:42 00:03:31:37 00:03:34:42
* FROM CLIP NAME: WHAT BLOOD DOES
* VISUAL: A body map with red delivery routes running to every organ
* NARRATION: Think about what your blood is actually responsible for in your body.

062  AX       V     C        00:03:34:42 00:03:38:34 00:03:34:42 00:03:38:34
* FROM CLIP NAME: EVERY SINGLE CELL
* VISUAL: Delivery trucks of oxygen travelling from brain down to fingertips
* NARRATION: Every single cell, from your brain to your fingertips, depends on blood arriving on time.

063  AX       V     C        00:03:38:34 00:03:41:54 00:03:38:34 00:03:41:54
* FROM CLIP NAME: OXYGEN AND NUTRIENTS
* VISUAL: Oxygen parcels being dropped off at tiny doorways all over the body
* NARRATION: Carrying oxygen and nutrients to every corner that is quietly waiting for them.

064  AX       V     C        00:03:41:54 00:03:44:59 00:03:41:54 00:03:44:59
* FROM CLIP NAME: EVERYTHING DOWNSTREAM
* VISUAL: A delivery route with a roadblock, everything behind it backing up
* NARRATION: When that flow is even slightly restricted, everything downstream feels it immediately.

065  AX       V     C        00:03:44:59 00:03:48:05 00:03:44:59 00:03:48:05
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE 3PM SLUMP
* VISUAL: A clock at three in the afternoon with a brain battery draining
* NARRATION: Even if you cannot explain why your focus fades every single afternoon.

066  AX       V     C        00:03:48:05 00:03:51:41 00:03:48:05 00:03:51:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: COLD HANDS
* VISUAL: Blue tinted hands and feet with a thermometer reading low
* NARRATION: Or why your hands and feet always seem a little colder than everyone else's.

067  AX       V     C        00:03:51:41 00:03:54:46 00:03:51:41 00:03:54:46
* FROM CLIP NAME: FOUR STEPS
* VISUAL: A bold title card with four numbered boxes in hand drawn capitals
* NARRATION: So what do you actually do with this? Four things. Simple. Specific.

068  AX       V     C        00:03:54:46 00:03:58:38 00:03:54:46 00:03:58:38
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP ONE: RAW
* VISUAL: A raw onion with a tick beside a cooked onion with a cross
* NARRATION: First, eat onions raw, not cooked. Heat destroys both the quercetin and the sulfur compounds.

069  AX       V     C        00:03:58:38 00:04:02:29 00:03:58:38 00:04:02:29
* FROM CLIP NAME: BENEFIT GONE
* VISUAL: Soft sweet onions in a pan with the active compounds evaporating as steam
* NARRATION: If you only eat them soft and sweet, most of the benefit is already gone.

070  AX       V     C        00:04:02:29 00:04:06:21 00:04:02:29 00:04:06:21
* FROM CLIP NAME: ADD IT AFTER
* VISUAL: Raw onion slices being sprinkled onto a finished hot dish
* NARRATION: Add raw onion to salads, sandwiches, or as a topping after the cooking is done.

071  AX       V     C        00:04:06:21 00:04:09:26 00:04:06:21 00:04:09:26
* FROM CLIP NAME: AFTER, NEVER DURING
* VISUAL: A thermometer with a red never zone and a green after zone
* NARRATION: After the heat, never during it. That single change preserves almost everything.

072  AX       V     C        00:04:09:26 00:04:12:47 00:04:09:26 00:04:12:47
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP TWO: RED OR YELLOW
* VISUAL: Red and yellow onions with a tick, white onion crossed out
* NARRATION: Second, choose red or yellow onions over the white ones every single time.

073  AX       V     C        00:04:12:47 00:04:16:07 00:04:12:47 00:04:16:07
* FROM CLIP NAME: DEEPER IS BETTER
* VISUAL: A colour gradient from white to deep red with quercetin bars rising
* NARRATION: The deeper the colour, the higher the quercetin content. That is not tradition.

074  AX       V     C        00:04:16:07 00:04:19:43 00:04:16:07 00:04:19:43
* FROM CLIP NAME: IT'S CHEMISTRY
* VISUAL: A chef's hat and a storybook crossed out, a chemistry flask highlighted
* NARRATION: It is not a chef's preference or an old wives' tale. It is chemistry.

075  AX       V     C        00:04:19:43 00:04:22:49 00:04:19:43 00:04:22:49
* FROM CLIP NAME: PACKED INSIDE
* VISUAL: A dark red onion cross-section glowing with protective compound dots
* NARRATION: Darker skin means more protective plant compounds are packed inside that bulb.

076  AX       V     C        00:04:22:49 00:04:26:25 00:04:22:49 00:04:26:25
* FROM CLIP NAME: READ THE COLOUR
* VISUAL: A shopper in a produce aisle reading onion colours as a nutrition label
* NARRATION: When you stand in the produce aisle, read the colour like a nutrition label.

077  AX       V     C        00:04:26:25 00:04:30:01 00:04:26:25 00:04:30:01
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP THREE: ADD FAT
* VISUAL: An olive oil bottle pouring gently over a bowl of raw onion
* NARRATION: Third, pair your onions with a small amount of healthy fat, like olive oil.

078  AX       V     C        00:04:30:01 00:04:33:21 00:04:30:01 00:04:33:21
* FROM CLIP NAME: FAT SOLUBLE
* VISUAL: Quercetin molecules hitching a ride on fat droplets into the bloodstream
* NARRATION: Quercetin is fat soluble, so your body absorbs significantly more with fat present.

079  AX       V     C        00:04:33:21 00:04:36:57 00:04:33:21 00:04:36:57
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT JUST A RECIPE
* VISUAL: A bowl of onion, tomato, olive oil and lemon arranged neatly
* NARRATION: Raw onion, tomatoes, olive oil, a little lemon. That is not just a recipe.

080  AX       V     C        00:04:36:57 00:04:40:17 00:04:36:57 00:04:40:17
* FROM CLIP NAME: A DELIVERY SYSTEM
* VISUAL: The salad bowl turning into a rocket delivering compounds into a vessel
* NARRATION: It is a delivery system built to get that compound into your bloodstream.

081  AX       V     C        00:04:40:17 00:04:43:38 00:04:40:17 00:04:43:38
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP FOUR: WAIT 10 MIN
* VISUAL: Chopped onion on a board beside a timer counting down ten minutes
* NARRATION: Fourth, let your chopped onion sit for ten minutes before you eat it.

082  AX       V     C        00:04:43:38 00:04:47:14 00:04:43:38 00:04:47:14
* FROM CLIP NAME: LET THE ENZYME WORK
* VISUAL: A tiny enzyme worker inside the onion completing a chemical assembly line
* NARRATION: That short window gives an enzyme inside the onion time to finish its work.

083  AX       V     C        00:04:47:14 00:04:51:05 00:04:47:14 00:04:51:05
* FROM CLIP NAME: CUT, REST, EAT
* VISUAL: Three step icons: chop, rest, eat, with a green completion tick
* NARRATION: Cut it, let it rest, then eat it. Ten minutes is all the chemistry needs.

084  AX       V     C        00:04:51:05 00:04:54:41 00:04:51:05 00:04:54:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOBODY SAYS IT
* VISUAL: A tall stack of research papers with a tiny megaphone beside them
* NARRATION: This is in the scientific literature, but almost nobody communicates it to ordinary people.

085  AX       V     C        00:04:54:41 00:04:58:48 00:04:54:41 00:04:58:48
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE MISSION
* VISUAL: A bridge being built between a laboratory and an ordinary home kitchen
* NARRATION: Getting this information to the people who need it is what Food Code exists to do.

086  AX       V     C        00:04:58:48 00:05:02:08 00:04:58:48 00:05:02:08
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU CHANGED
* VISUAL: A person transformed, glowing brain, looking thoughtfully at an onion
* NARRATION: You are not someone who eats onions just because they taste good anymore.

087  AX       V     C        00:05:02:08 00:05:06:00 00:05:02:08 00:05:06:00
* FROM CLIP NAME: CELLULAR LEVEL
